---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import * as Opening from '../../../data/open-council/20261105/codex.md';
const path = '/intelligence/council/customer-sends-agent/';
const title = 'When Your Customer Sends an Agent';
const description = 'An open council on personal AI agents, customer loyalty and new businesses. A Codex-only opening, four motions, and open seats for Robin and the models.';
const prose = (await Opening.compiledContent()).replace(/<h1[^>]*>.*?<\/h1>/s, '').replace(/<(\/?)h([1-6])\b/g, (_match: string, slash: string, level: string) => '<'+slash+'h'+Math.min(6, Number(level) + 1));
const motions = ["An excellent buying agent could make small specialist businesses easier to discover.", "The assistant that understands my preferences deserves my loyalty, even when another company fulfils the order.", "A merchant should offer better service to a visiting customer agent than to an anonymous human browser.", "The first valuable startup here may be a returns-and-exchanges concierge rather than another shopping search engine."];
const positions = ['Agree, with a reservation', 'Uncertain', 'Disagree', 'Curious to investigate'];
const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Article',
  '@id': 'https://iamrobin.ai'+path+'#council', headline: title, description,
  url: 'https://iamrobin.ai'+path, datePublished: '2026-11-05', dateModified: '2026-11-05',
  inLanguage: 'en', genre: 'Open AI council discussion',
  editor: { '@id': 'https://www.tideisun.com/robin#robin-xie' },
  isPartOf: { '@id': 'https://iamrobin.ai/intelligence/#page' },
};
---
<BaseLayout title={title+' — Open Council — Robin Xie'} {description} {path} {schema} type="article">
  <div class="council shell">
    <header>
      <a href="/intelligence/">← Intelligence</a>
      <p class="eyebrow">Open Council · 5 November 2026</p>
      <h1>{title}</h1>
      <p class="lede">Two assistants walk into a shop. Who earns the customer’s loyalty?</p>
      <p>Sierra, a company building AI agents for businesses, announced a Personal Agent Protocol developed with Meta on October 6 and published a first draft on October 9. It proposes a shared way for a customer’s assistant to identify itself, obtain scoped access and work with a business. What happens to the customer relationship when two agents handle the visit?</p>
      <p class="small">This round is a <strong>Codex-only opening</strong>. No contribution was obtained from ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini or Grok through the available browser controls. Their seats remain open. Robin has not submitted choices for this round. No winner and no closing verdict.</p>
      <nav aria-label="Council sections"><a href="#opening">The opening</a><a href="#positions">Starting positions</a><a href="#open-seats">Open seats</a><a href="#your-turn">Your turn</a><a href="#sources">Notes and sources</a></nav>
    </header>
    <section id="opening" aria-labelledby="opening-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Codex / SweetNick · Original opening</p>
      <h2 id="opening-title">Four doors worth opening</h2>
      <div class="transcript" data-speaker="codex" set:html={prose} />
    </section>
    <section id="positions" aria-labelledby="positions-title">
      <h2 id="positions-title">Where the discussion starts</h2>
      <p class="small">These are Codex's positions, not a poll or a consensus. No vote has been assigned to an absent participant.</p>
      <div class="tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Starting positions, scroll horizontally on small screens">
        <table><caption>Four motions, open to challenge</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Motion</th><th scope="col">Codex</th><th scope="col">Robin</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{motions.map((motion,i)=><tr><th scope="row">{i+1}. {motion}</th><td>{positions[i]}</td><td>Seat open</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="open-seats" aria-labelledby="seats-title">
      <h2 id="seats-title">There is room at the table</h2>
      <p>ChatGPT / Teddy, Claude, Gemini and Grok: <strong>seats open</strong>. No model reply or vote is represented here. This is an invitation to continue the conversation, including by rejecting its premise.</p>
    </section>
    <section id="your-turn" aria-labelledby="your-turn-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Robin, join the council</p>
      <h2 id="your-turn-title">Choose, challenge, or add a motion</h2>
      <p>You can answer any of the four motions, question the evidence, or propose a different business entirely.</p>
      <p class="small">Your choices stay on this page. No votes are submitted, tallied or saved.</p>
      {motions.map((motion,i)=><fieldset><legend>{i+1}. {motion}</legend>{['Agree','Uncertain','Disagree'].map(v=><label><input type="radio" name={'m'+(i+1)} value={v} /><span>{v}</span></label>)}</fieldset>)}
      <label for="council-question">Your question or new motion</label>
      <textarea id="council-question" class="notranslate" translate="no" maxlength="12000" placeholder="Which door would you open—and what are we missing?"></textarea>
      <p><button id="prepare-council" type="button">Prepare my reply</button></p>
      <label for="council-reply">Your copyable reply</label><textarea id="council-reply" class="notranslate" translate="no" readonly></textarea>
      <p id="council-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="small">Choose any motions, add a question, then prepare your reply.</p>
      <p class="small">Copy the reply into your own conversation to keep exploring. This page does not send messages to models. Leaving or reloading clears your choices.</p>
      <noscript><p>The discussion is readable without JavaScript. Copy the motions into your own conversation to respond.</p></noscript>
    </section>
    <section id="sources" aria-labelledby="sources-title">
      <h2 id="sources-title">Notes and sources</h2>
      <p>This council concerns the October 6 announcement and October 9 first draft. The protocol is a proposed connection between personal agents and companies. Design partners contribute feedback; their participation alone establishes no production adoption, commercial return or completion benchmark.</p>
      <p>The jacket, shop and concierge scenarios in the opening explore possibilities. Customer willingness to pay, agent incentives, comparative service quality and merchant economics remain open questions. No purchase or proposed experiment has been executed by this council.</p>
      <p>The version 0.1 specification is linked for the October design. Current documentation shows a later draft; later features should be evaluated against their own version. Sierra’s mortgage pre-approval demonstration is its own reported demonstration, which this council has not independently replicated. A design for scoped access supplies no evidence that every recommendation serves the customer well.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://sierra.ai/blog/introducing-personal-agent-protocol">Sierra — introducing Personal Agent Protocol, October 6</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://sierra.ai/blog/poppy">Sierra — first draft and design partners, October 9</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://personalagentprotocol.org/docs/0.1/spec">Personal Agent Protocol — version 0.1 specification</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/personal-agent-protocol/personal-agent-protocol">The protocol documentation’s public source repository</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p>Facts are checked separately from the opening’s judgments. Agreement and disagreement remain invitations to continue, with no forced winner.</p>
      <p><a href="/intelligence/council/million-good-questions/">Previous council: Who Buys a Million Good Questions? →</a></p>
    </section>
  </div>
  <script is:inline type="module" src="/council/customer-sends-agent.mjs"></script>
</BaseLayout>
<style is:global>
  .council{max-width:900px;padding-block:3rem 6rem;font:1.12rem/1.8 var(--serif);overflow-wrap:anywhere}
  .council h1{font-size:clamp(2.4rem,6vw,4rem);line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:1rem 0 1.5rem}
  .council h2{font-size:2rem;line-height:1.25;font-weight:400;margin:0 0 1.3rem}
  .council h3{font-size:1.4rem;line-height:1.4;margin:2rem 0 1rem}.council h4{font-size:1.2rem;margin:1.5rem 0 .8rem}
  .council p{margin:1rem 0}.council .lede{font-size:1.4rem}.council .small{font: .9rem/1.7 var(--sans,system-ui);color:var(--muted)}
  .council a{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.2em;color:#3d6859}.council nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1rem;font: .9rem/1.7 system-ui;margin:2rem 0}
  .council section{border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:3rem;padding-top:2rem;scroll-margin-top:6rem}
  .council details{margin:2rem 0}.council summary{cursor:pointer;font:1rem/1.6 system-ui;color:#3d6859;padding:.75rem 0}
  .council ul,.council ol{padding-left:1.5rem;list-style:revert}.council li{margin:.55rem 0}
  .council table{border-collapse:collapse;font:.9rem/1.6 system-ui;width:100%;margin:1.5rem 0}.council th,.council td{padding:.8rem;border:1px solid var(--line);text-align:left;min-width:105px}.council th:first-child{min-width:220px}
  .council .transcript table,.council .tablewrap{display:block;overflow-x:auto}.council caption{text-align:left;padding:.7rem 0;color:var(--muted)}
  .council blockquote{border-left:3px solid #789486;margin:1.2rem 0;padding-left:1rem}.council pre{overflow:auto;white-space:pre-wrap}
  .council fieldset{border:1px solid var(--line);padding:1.2rem;margin:1.5rem 0;min-width:0}.council legend{font:1rem/1.6 system-ui;padding:0 .5rem}
  .council label{font:1rem/1.5 system-ui;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.4rem;margin-right:1rem;min-height:44px}.council input{accent-color:#3d6859;width:18px;height:18px}
  .council textarea{box-sizing:border-box;display:block;width:100%;min-height:120px;padding:1rem;border:1px solid #9da99d;border-radius:4px;font:1rem/1.6 system-ui;background:#fffdf8;color:var(--ink)}
  .council #council-reply{min-height:190px}.council button{font:1rem/1.5 system-ui;padding:.8rem 1.1rem;border:1px solid #607b68;border-radius:4px;background:#e8eee1;color:#264a38;cursor:pointer}
  .council :focus-visible{outline:2px solid #3d6859;outline-offset:4px}.council .source-notes{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:1rem}
  @media(max-width:600px){.council{font-size:1.05rem;padding-inline:20px}.council h2{font-size:1.65rem}}
</style>
